  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 4-204(c)): (c) (1) (i) A person who violates this section is guilty of a [misdemeanor] FELONY and, in addition to any other penalty imposed for the crime of violence or felony, shall be sentenced: 2. FOR A SECOND OR SUBSEQUENT OFFENSE, TO IMPRISONMENT FOR NOT LESS THAN 10 YEARS AND NOT EXCEEDING 40 YEARS.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 4-204(c)): 2. THE COURT MAY NOT IMPOSE LESS THAN THE MINIMUM SENTENCE OF 10 YEARS FOR A SENTENCE IMPOSED UNDER ITEM (I)2 OF THIS PARAGRAPH.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 5-621(c)): (ii) for each subsequent violation, imprisonment for not less than 10 years and not exceeding 40 years.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 5-621(c)): (ii) The court shall impose a minimum sentence of 10 years under paragraph (1)(ii) of this subsection.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 14-101(a)): (15) POSSESSING, USING, WEARING, CARRYING, OR TRANSPORTING A FIREARM DURING AND IN RELATION TO A DRUG TRAFFICKING CRIME UNDER § 5–621 OF THIS ARTICLE;\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-133(c)): (ii) a violation of § 5–602, § 5–603, § 5–604, § 5–605, § 5–612, § 5–613, § 5–614, § 5–621, OR § 5–622 of the Criminal Law Article;\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-133(c)): (3) EACH VIOLATION OF THIS SUBSECTION IS A SEPARATE CRIME."
